    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-3180",
      "problem": "What is the radius $r$ of a circle with a circumference of $C=17\\pi?$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14183030/assets/697cc9ca06bcfe46d84dfab74e0f6ae83f4342607ea4af138b111606c16e8a03.png)",
      "worked_solution": "We use the formula for the circumference $C=2\\pi r$ and solve for $r.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =2\\pi r \\\\ 17\\pi  & =2\\pi r \\\\ r & =\\frac{17\\pi }{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{2} \\\\  & =8.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
